~

@7053 = ~Sunblade: Daystar
Whether created specifically for use in the service of Torm or appropriated at some point in the long history of the church, paladins of the Loyal Fury have made good use of Daystar in their battles against evil undead. Through magic or blessing it is empowered with the Sunray, a force of pure life energy so potent that it slays both living and unliving.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Sunray once per day

THAC0: +2, +4 vs. evil creatures
Damage: 1d8+2, +4 vs. evil creatures, does double damage against undead
Damage type: Slashing
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Long Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 2~

@7054 = ~This helm is made of polished steel and set with diamonds, rubies, and fire opals. The gems glow with an internal light, the source of which can only be magical. The helm makes the wearer resistant to fire as well as giving the wearer some spell abilities. These include Fireball, Prismatic Spray, and Sunray.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Fire Resistance: +40%
– Protects against critical hits

Charge abilities:
– Fireball once per day
  Damage: 6d6 fire (Save vs. Wand for half)
  Range: 90 ft.
  Area: 15-ft. radius

– Prismatic Spray once per day
  Effects vary as per the 7th-level wizard spell

– Sunray once per day
  Effects vary as per the 7th-level cleric spell

Weight: 2~

@7055 = ~The master smith who forged this weapon, as skilled as he may be, has no clue why it took on a dark red colour very reminiscent of blood, complete from hilt to blade. After some pondering, he quietly warns you: "This powerful axe is evil". Combined from parts of cursed weapons worn by deranged warriors and strengthened with potent potions of barbarian essence, it emanates a sense of doom and disaster. Only someone who feels no mercy or remorse whatsoever would be capable of wielding it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Strength: +2
– Constitution: +2
– Wearer does not become winded after berserking
- Wearer does not get tired from using any spells and abilities

Combat abilities:
– Hit target must save vs. Death or be knocked down and take 2d6 extra crushing damage

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d8+5
Damage type: slashing
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 18 Strength

Weight: 1~

@7056 = ~Treefolk's Fist +4

Treefolk's Arm has been further strengthed and is an even more impressive weapon to defend nature.

STATISTICS:

Equipped ability:
+1 bonus to Strength

THAC0: +4, +6 vs. unnatural creatures
Damage: 1D6 +6, +8 vs. unnatural creatures
5% chance to inflict 20 points of acid damage on hit
5% chance to inflict 20 points of poison damage on hit

Damage type: Crushing
Weight: 3
Speed Factor: 3
