@7063 = ~Atonement involves making reparations, paying a price. The Cloak of Atonement takes this requirement literally. In exchange for protection and safety, it will leech the health of its wearer to power itself.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities (up to 5 charges each):
– instant cast of Armor of Faith and Chant at level 15 on self
  constitution score reduced by 2 points for 8 hours

- instant cast of Death Ward and Chaotic Commands at level 15 on self
  constitution score reduced by 3 points for 8 hours
  
- instant cast of Shield of Archons on self
  constitution score reduced by 4 points for 8 hours

The item does not disappear, when all of its charges are used.

Weight: 3~

@7064 = ~Assassin's Dream +5~

@7065 = ~Assassin's Dream +5

Stories tell of daggers wielded by the most infamous thieves and assassins of the Realms, each imbued with a fragment of their wielder's cunning, precision, and malice. Over decades, these weapons absorbed the essence of their masters, carrying echoes of their infamous deeds.

With the help of the Manual of Elaboration, master craftsman was able to extract and weave their lingering magical auras into a single blade. The result is this dagger, a creation not of steel and shards but of pure essence. When held, the weapon seems to move with a will of its own, subtly guiding its owner's hand with the wisdom of long-dead assassins.

To wield this blade is to carry the weight of countless lives taken and to feel the shadows of its former masters at your side. It is said that those who hold it too long may find their own spirit overshadowed by the whispers of the past.

The already powerful Assassin's Dream +4 has been upgraded to this fabulous weapon, which is undoubtedly the most fearsome blade in hands of a thief or an assassin.

STATISTICS:
- Can only be wielded in main hand

Equipped abilities:
- Stealth Strike +50% when used as a single weapon or with a shield
- +1 Attack per round, when used as a single weapon or with a shield
- Immunity to Poison and Backstab
- 5% on any hit to turn the wielder invisible for 1-turn.

Special ability:
Assassination: Twice per day

THAC0: +5 bonus
Damage: 2D4 +5
Damage type: piercing
Weight: 1
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: 1-handed
Require: 3 Strength~

@7066 = ~Bracers of Brute Force~

@7067 = ~Bracers of Brute Force
Though deceptively elegant in design, these heavy metal wristbands are etched with ancient sigils of war and rage. Worn by a long-forgotten duelist who favored brute strength over finesse, they channel raw power into each blow. However, their unbalanced weight and aggressive enchantment throw off the wearer's aim, making precision strikes more difficult.

STATISTICS:

+2 bonus to melee damage
–2 penalty to THAC0

Weight: 2~

@7068 = ~These gauntlets assist in the stalking and killing of prey. Favored by hunters of all kinds, they display their full power when donned by a Stalker. Made of supple leather with brass-buckled straps along the side, these gauntlets are often decorated with embroidered figures of stags, foxes, or, as is the case with this pair, wolves.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Dexterity: +1
– Hide in Shadows: +10%
– Stealth Strike: +10% (Stalkers only)

Weight: 2~

